Approach: Implement Queue Using Two Stacks
The idea is to implement FIFO (First In, First Out) behavior of a queue using stacks, which normally follow LIFO (Last In, First Out).

We use two stacks:

s1 → stores elements in queue order
s2 → temporary stack used while inserting
The important trick is to always keep the front element at the top of s1.

1. push(x)
Normally, a stack puts the new element on top.

But for a queue, the oldest element must stay on top.

Suppose:

Queue: 1 → 2 → 3

We want 1 to be at the top of s1:

